{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md | sed -n '1,350p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# dao.stream.host-boundary: dao.stream wherever the boundary can be an IO action\n     2\t\n     3\tThe governing test is the owner's: **dao.stream is used wherever a host\n     4\tboundary can be an IO action; a pure, total, synchronous function on the same\n     5\thost may be a direct call.** Under it, every contact between the portable\n     6\tcore and a host is either a `dao.stream` implementation's host seam (the IO\n     7\tactions: sockets, files, locks, clock, entropy, another process) or one entry\n     8\tof an exact, enumerated primitive profile (the pure functions: carriers,\n     9\thashing, signing, canonical encoding) with a named oracle. Porting a host is:\n    10\timplement the stream seams the composition selects, implement the primitive\n    11\tprofile against the oracles, write a `main`.\n    12\t\n    13\tStatus: design only; nothing commissioned. **Revision r2**, 2026-10-20, by\n    14\tthe Architect (claude-fable-5-1). r1 rationale:\n    15\t`collab/1792495909000-architect-host-boundary.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md`.\n    16\tr1 was reviewed NOT SIGNED OFF by a non-Claude architect\n    17\t(`collab/1792498045000-architect-host-boundary-review.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`,\n    18\tfindings A1-A8); r2 answers each (rationale and disposition table in\n    19\t`collab/1792502807000-architect-host-boundary-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md`)\n    20\tand records the owner's refined rule and six adopted decisions (§11.1). No\n    21\tcode was changed; every claim about the tree is labelled. **Because this\n    22\tdocument was written by a Claude model, a non-Claude architect must sign it\n    23\toff again before anything is commissioned from it or relied on** (§13).\n    24\t\n    25\tOwner direction, verbatim. Original (the \"maybe\" is the owner's): \"maybe this\n    26\tis an opportunity to stop and refactor so that the dao.stream is the boundary\n    27\tthat crosses over host specific dependency. once that is done, the only thing\n    28\tneeds porting is dao.stream implementations\". Refined, after r1: \"maybe my\n    29\tdao.stream ABI framing has to be refined.  when a host-boundary is cross\n    30\tshould it be used. when its on the same host, then direct function call is\n    31\tfine. In other words, when the host boundary can be an IO monad then\n    32\tdao.stream is used. If it cannot be a monad than dao.stream doesnt have to be\n    33\tused\". Asked which formulation governs, the owner answered \"yes, test 2\n    34\tgoverns\": the operative rule is the IO-action test, not same-host-ness. A\n    35\tsame-host effect (a file read, a clock reading, entropy) is still an IO\n    36\taction and so a stream.\n    37\t\n    38\tAuthorities:\n    39\t- [datom.world.md](./datom.world.md) `:43-48` and `:70`.\n    40\t- [datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md) §3 (custody), §4 (machine-\n    41\t  internal work executes inside the instance; only effects and facts cross),\n    42\t  §5 (the floor is world facts; internal linkage is not a boundary), §6\n    43\t  (effects out, events in), §7 (adapter discipline; `:143-148`, the two\n    44\t  things that are not adapters). §12 proposes the amendment that records the\n    45\t  refined rule there; nothing in this document edits it.\n    46\t- [dao.stream.md](./dao.stream.md): the contract.\n    47\t- [dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md) §1 `:29-52`: the seven imports;\n    48\t  no second ABI; park, resume, primitives and state reads have no imports.\n    49\t- [dao.stream.codec.md](./dao.stream.codec.md): the transport codec track,\n    50\t  another orchestrator's; this document builds on it and touches none of its\n    51\t  files while its slices are in flight (§8).\n    52\t- [yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.5: the conformance method.\n    53\t- [dao.jing.md](./dao.jing.md), [dao.jing.cbor.md](./dao.jing.cbor.md).\n    54\t\n    55\tLabels: V = verified by reading this tree on 2026-10-20 (line cites); R =\n    56\tread or inferred from a report or log, not run; P = proposed, does not exist\n    57\tyet. Nothing was executed.\n    58\t\n    59\tThis document is standalone. A future host lane (a native Clojure dialect on\n    60\ta Scheme runtime, a Rust peer, a wasm instance) is an example consumer of it,\n    61\tnever a dependency of it.\n    62\t\n    63\t---\n    64\t\n    65\t## 1. Problem\n    66\t\n    67\tV: the portable core (`src/cljc`, 183 files) reaches hosts two ways and the\n    68\tdoctrine sanctions only one. The sanctioned way is the transports' pattern: a\n    69\tportable core under `src/cljc/dao/stream/` plus a per-host seam under\n    70\t`src/clj`, `src/cljs`, `src/cljd` (`ws/jvm.clj` 471 lines, `ws/node.cljs` 340,\n    71\t`ws/dart.cljd` 339, `ws/browser.cljs` 112; `datagram/jvm.clj` 111,\n    72\t`datagram/node.cljs` 110, `datagram/dart.cljd` 173; `waitset/driver.*`\n    73\t49/80/79). The seam is a plain map of functions the composition hands in\n    74\t(`yin.repl.host/websocket`, `src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc:20-37`;\n    75\t`dao.stream.datagram.jvm/bind!`, `jvm.clj:22-34`). The core names no socket\n    76\tlibrary.\n    77\t\n    78\tThe other way is host contact inside portable files: reader-conditional arms\n    79\tthat reach a host library, and, invisibly to a reader-conditional census,\n    80\t**resolved calls to host-backed core functions** (`random-uuid`, `rand`,\n    81\t`gensym`, `System/getProperty`, `println`) that compile on every host and\n    82\tstill touch the world (review A3). §3.2 is the census by resolved calls.\n    83\t\n    84\tV, `rg -c '#\\?'` over `src/cljc` (every conditional, harmless arms included):\n    85\t\n    86\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n    87\t| File                              | `#?`  | What the arms reach (V)                                                                                 |\n    88\t+===================================+=======+=========================================================================================================+\n    89\t| `dao/jing/cbor.cljc` (1562 lines) | 52    | `BigInteger`/JS `BigInt`/Dart `BigInt` helpers (`:106-254`), float bit extraction (`:525-560`), the     |\n    90\t|                                   |       | `Float64`, `Rational`, `Decimal` carrier types (`:342-450`, protocol arms for equality, hashing and     |\n    91\t|                                   |       | printing), the wire writer namespace (`:58-60`: Boring on JVM and JS, the `cbor` Dart package).         |\n    92\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n    93\t| `dao/data/btree.cljc` (2158)      | 35    | Host arrays via `dao.data.arrays` (21 arms; `Arrays/parallelSort` at `:145`); `AtomicBoolean` for       |\n    94\t|                                   |       | transient ownership (`:103-119`); weak and soft references for the node cache (`:211-245`).             |\n    95\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n    96\t| `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (299)  | 30    | The declared integer shim: 25 public functions (`:41-298`).                                              |\n    97\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n    98\t| `dao/jing/file.cljc` (455)        | 19    | Random-access file: open, length, read-int, read-bytes, truncate, append, sync, close (`:159-259`);      |\n    99\t|                                   |       | `locking` on the JVM (`:338`).                                                                          |\n   100\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   101\t| `dao/space/store/fs.cljc` (494)   | 17    | Directory lock: `FileChannel.tryLock`, Dart `lockSync`, Node claim files with pid liveness (`:87-224`);  |\n   102\t|                                   |       | temp write, fsync, rename (`:352-378`); directory sync (`:265-314`); `os.name`/`platform` (`:271-273`). |\n   103\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   104\t| `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (274)   | 16    | Ed25519 via `java.security`, `ed25519_edwards`, a JS library; `SecureRandom` for seeds (`:79,:120`).    |\n   105\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   106\t| `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (132) | 14    | Every form `:cljd nil`-gated; wraps `boring.core/encode`.                                                |\n   107\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   108\t| `dao/jing.cljc` (629)             | 12    | BLAKE3 and SHA-256 libraries (`:32-40, :59-135`); an opaque sentinel object (`:43-51`).                  |\n   109\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   110\t| `yin/vm/values.cljc` (9)          | 9     | `Closure` and `Continuation` types with per-host equality, hashing and printing arms (`:39-119`).       |\n   111\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   112\t| `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc` (16)       | 16    | Bytes predicate, char access, NFC (`java.text.Normalizer`, `String.normalize`, `unorm_dart`, `:310-321`,|\n   113\t|                                   |       | Unicode 16.0 owner-settled), float64 bits, carrier tests.                                               |\n   114\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   115\t| `yin/repl/main.cljc` (15)         | 15    | The driver: clock, `Thread` pollers, stdin/stdout, `process.exit`, `user.home` (`:348-1542`).            |\n   116\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   117\t| `dao/stream/codec.cljc` (4),      | 4+4+5 | Host number and bytes predicates (`codec.cljc:19,45`); base64 libraries; `Uint8List` length, alloc,    |\n   118\t| `base64.cljc`, `chunks.cljc`      |       | slice, copy (`chunks.cljc:8-32`).                                                                       |\n   119\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   120\t| `dao/jing/dht.cljc` (10),         | 10+7  | Bytes helpers (`dht.cljc:100-121`); `secure-random-bytes` (`space/dht.cljc:142-151`); the datagram seam |\n   121\t| `dao/space/dht.cljc`              |       | selected by reader arm (`:132-139`).                                                                    |\n   122\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   123\t| `dao/jing/content/async.cljc` (3),| 3+4   | A timer per host inside a portable file (`async.cljc:47-58`) that re-enters the pump (`:100-149`);     |\n   124\t| `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc`     |       | a host promise type (`CompletableFuture`, `js/Promise`, Dart `Future`) as the async facade              |\n   125\t|                                   |       | (`storage.cljc:218-227`).                                                                               |\n   126\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   127\t| `yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc`   | 6     | Generated ANTLR recognizers per host; `yang.antlr.cst` per host (`src/clj` 221, `src/cljs` 200,         |\n   128\t| (6)                               |       | `src/cljd` 203 lines).                                                                                  |\n   129\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   130\t| Remaining files (about 40)        | 1-15  | Dialect syntax: `catch` type arms, `^long` hints, protocol names, `exists?`. No host library (§3.3).     |\n   131\t+-----------------------------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   132\t\n   133\tR (a spike that brought the core up on a fourth host): 86 of the 91\n   134\tnamespaces in the `yin.repl` closure loaded unchanged; the failures were the\n   135\trows above (integer shim, Jing hashing, the Boring writer, the file and store\n   136\tnamespaces, `parallelSort`, the Java ANTLR parser). V, the duplication:\n   137\t`yin.vm.integer.host` says it \"does not reach into `dao.jing.cbor`'s private\n   138\tbig-integer helpers\" (`host.cljc:23-25`), and `dao.jing.cbor` keeps its own\n   139\t(`cbor.cljc:112-216`). Two shims, one contract.\n   140\t\n   141\t## 2. The governing rule\n   142\t\n   143\t### 2.1 Statement\n   144\t\n   145\t**A host contact uses `dao.stream` if and only if it can be an IO action. A\n   146\thost contact that cannot be an IO action, because it is a pure, total,\n   147\tsynchronous function of its arguments executed on the same host, may be a\n   148\tdirect function call, and is then an entry of the primitive profile (§4.3).**\n   149\t\n   150\tThis is the owner's test 2, verbatim in the header. Same-host-ness is not the\n   151\tcriterion: a same-host file read is an IO action and is a stream; a\n   152\tcryptographic hash from a library linked into the same host is not an IO\n   153\taction and is a direct call.\n   154\t\n   155\t### 2.2 \"Can be an IO action\", operationally\n   156\t\n   157\tA contact **can be an IO action** when any of the following holds. Each is a\n   158\tproperty the doctrine already names, cited.\n   159\t\n   160\t+----+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   161\t| #  | Property                      | Meaning, and the doctrine that names it                                                                     |\n   162\t+====+===============================+=============================================================================================================+\n   163\t| 1  | Observation of the world      | The result depends on something other than the arguments: a file, a socket, another process, the           |\n   164\t|    |                               | environment, a resource's current state. `abi.md` §5: \"world facts that shipped code cannot compute\".        |\n   165\t+----+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   166\t| 2  | Effect on the world           | Calling it changes something outside the machine's own values: bytes on disk, a packet sent, a lock taken,   |\n   167\t|    |                               | text printed. `datom.world.md:46`: \"Side effects must appear as stream emissions.\"                           |\n   168\t+----+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   169\t| 3  | Nondeterminism                | Two calls with equal arguments may answer differently: entropy, a clock, a process-wide counter, a host      |\n   170\t|    |                               | object's identity. The answer is a fact about the world or the run, not about the arguments.                 |\n   171\t+----+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   172\t| 4  | Asynchrony                    | The answer is not available when the call returns, or completion invokes something later: a timer, a        |\n   173\t|    |                               | thread, a promise. `dao.stream.md`: \"No operation waits\"; `abi.md` §6: a callback is an event on a stream.   |\n   174\t+----+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   175\t| 5  | World-dependent failure       | Whether it completes depends on the world (a disk full, a peer gone), as opposed to on the input.            |\n   176\t|    |                               | `dao.stream.md`, Result Convention: such outcomes are data, never exceptions.                                |\n   177\t+----+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   178\t| 6  | Another process or host       | The work runs in a different process, machine or trust domain. `abi.md` §3: custody.                        |\n   179\t+----+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   180\t\n   181\tA contact **cannot be an IO action** when none holds: the result is a total,\n   182\tdeterministic function of its arguments, computed synchronously in the same\n   183\tprocess, and its only failures are functions of the input (malformed input)\n   184\tanswered as data or a refusal. Linking a library to compute such a function is\n   185\t\"internal compiler linkage\", which \"does not create an ecosystem boundary\"\n   186\t(`abi.md` §5, `:80-81`); executing it is \"machine-internal work\" that\n   187\t\"executes inside the instance\" (`abi.md` §4, `:60-62`). That is the basis for\n   188\tthe primitive profile: **purity, totality and synchrony**, not frequency and\n   189\tnot \"it is internal\" by fiat (review A1). Frequency decides nothing; it is\n   190\tonly why the rule matters for performance (§2.4).\n   191\t\n   192\t### 2.3 Borderline cases, decided\n   193\t\n   194\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   195\t| Case                              | Reasoning under §2.2                                                                                    | Verdict    |\n   196\t+===================================+=========================================================================================================+============+\n   197\t| UTF-8 decode, CBOR decode, base64 | Fallible, but the failure is a function of the input bytes, not of the world (property 5 does not       | Direct     |\n   198\t| decode, NFC normalization         | hold); deterministic, synchronous. Malformed input is a refusal value. NFC depends on a Unicode version, | call       |\n   199\t|                                   | which the profile pins (16.0, V `debruijn.cljc:314`) so the function stays deterministic across hosts.   |            |\n   200\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   201\t| Hashing or signing in an external | A deterministic function of bytes (and, for signing, of the seed). The library is linkage (`abi.md`     | Direct     |\n   202\t| library (BLAKE3, SHA-256,         | §5). It must execute **in the same instance**: for wasm that means compiled in, never imported (§7),    | call, in-  |\n   203\t| Ed25519)                          | because an import is a host crossing and a crossing is a boundary whatever the function's purity (A1).  | instance   |\n   204\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   205\t| Key generation, nonces, secrets,  | Entropy: property 3. The portable core never reads a generator; it reads entropy that the driver         | Stream     |\n   206\t| fresh identities                  | deposited (§3.2, §4.4).                                                                                 |            |\n   207\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   208\t| Time                              | Property 3 and 1. A clock reading is an event the driver deposits or a value it passes as data; the      | Stream /   |\n   209\t|                                   | core never calls a clock (V: `dao.stream.ws/accept-connection!` already takes `now`, `ws.cljc:639`).    | data       |\n   210\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   211\t| Scheduling, timers, wake-up       | Property 4. The driver owns pumping and wake-up; the core exposes a step the driver calls. A thunk        | Driver     |\n   212\t|                                   | handed to a timer that re-enters the core is a relocated callback (`abi.md:146-148`), rejected (A2).     |            |\n   213\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   214\t| The Python parser                 | Two shapes. In-process, synchronous, deterministic over the source text and the pinned grammar: a pure    | Either;    |\n   215\t|                                   | function, direct call allowed. As another process or host (property 6): a stream. The stage shape         | the stage  |\n   216\t|                                   | (`parser.cljc:65-75`, V) carries both without change: source units in, CST packets out.                   | supports   |\n   217\t|                                   |                                                                                                         | both       |\n   218\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   219\t| Same-host file read, lock, fsync, | Properties 1, 2, 5. IO actions even though same-host; they sit under a stream implementation's seam       | Stream     |\n   220\t| rename, directory listing         | (§4.2). The owner's clarification names exactly this case.                                              |            |\n   221\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   222\t| Printing to stdout, reading stdin | Property 2 and 1. Driver IO.                                                                             | Driver     |\n   223\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   224\t| Weak and soft references, GC      | Dereferencing answers differently depending on the collector (property 3), but about the machine's own    | Runtime    |\n   225\t|                                   | memory, not the world. Not a boundary; a documented **runtime prerequisite** the dialect must provide     | prereq.    |\n   226\t|                                   | (§4.3, table C), with the strong-cache default so correctness never depends on it (V `btree.cljc:182`).  |            |\n   227\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   228\t| Atomics, `locking`, atoms,        | Machine-internal synchronization between threads the driver created. Not world contact. Runtime           | Runtime    |\n   229\t| volatiles                         | prerequisite; the core's single-owner discipline keeps them out of semantics.                            | prereq.    |\n   230\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   231\t| Host `=`, `hash`, `compare`,      | Pure functions of their arguments on one host, but **not identical across hosts** for mixed types and     | Dialect    |\n   232\t| `sort`, `str` of a double, regex  | floats. Not a boundary. A portability hazard the profile addresses only where bytes or addresses depend  | semantics  |\n   233\t|                                   | on it: Jing sorts by canonical bytes (V `cbor.cljc:1070,1177`), the UCF sorts by bytes (`rows.cljc:139`),|            |\n   234\t|                                   | the VM's float text is its own algorithm (`integer.cljc:51-60`). The remaining `sort-by str` sites order  |            |\n   235\t|                                   | diagnostics and iteration, not persisted bytes (§3.2 row 9).                                             |            |\n   236\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   237\t| `gensym` in a compiler            | Property 3 (a process-wide counter). Not world contact, but non-reproducible output. Classified as a      | Residual,  |\n   238\t| (`yang.clojure:349,359`,          | residual to remove by threading a counter through compiler state; assigned to H5.                        | H5         |\n   239\t| `yang.php:575`, `transact.cljc:35`|                                                                                                         |            |\n   240\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   241\t| Allocation, memory growth         | Machine-internal. Out of scope; a limit is a qualified local outcome (`dao.stream.wasm.md` §2).           | Not IO     |\n   242\t+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+\n   243\t\n   244\t### 2.4 Where the owner's original sentence is and is not met\n   245\t\n   246\t\"The only thing needs porting is dao.stream implementations\" is met for\n   247\t**every contact that can be an IO action**: after this design, a host's world\n   248\tcontact is exactly the stream seams of §4.1 and its `main`. It is **not met\n   249\tliterally**: a port also implements the primitive profile (§4.3) and the\n   250\truntime prerequisites (table C), because the dialect's own carriers (its\n   251\tintegers, bytes, strings, arrays) cannot be supplied by a stream and must not\n   252\tbe (a stream round trip per `integer/add` would turn the guest's inner loop\n   253\tinto IO). What the design does for that part is make it exact, enumerated,\n   254\tand oracle-checked, so a port implements a list, not a design. Review A1\n   255\tasked for this stated plainly; it is the honest scope.\n   256\t\n   257\t## 3. Reclassification of every host dependency\n   258\t\n   259\t### 3.1 By kind\n   260\t\n   261\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   262\t| Kind                             | Today (V)                                                 | §2 verdict  | Target                                                    |\n   263\t+==================================+===========================================================+=============+===========================================================+\n   264\t| Sockets (WebSocket, datagram,    | `dao.stream.ws`, `.datagram`, `.udp` portable; seams per  | IO (1,2,4,  | Unchanged. Seams named in §4.1; shared implementation     |\n   265\t| UDP)                             | host (§1).                                                | 5)          | conformance suite (§6).                                   |\n   266\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   267\t| Durable storage (content log,    | `dao.jing.file`, `dao.space.store.fs`, `dao.space.store`, | IO (1,2,5)  | The journal is already the stream (`journal/file.cljc`    |\n   268\t| lock, HEAD)                      | `dao.stream.journal.file`, `btree/storage`: 56 arms.      |             | `:1-23`). One seam beneath it, §4.2, with lower           |\n   269\t|                                  |                                                           |             | operations enumerated (A7).                               |\n   270\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   271\t| Entropy and fresh identities     | 25 resolved sites (§3.2 rows 1-2): `random-uuid` in       | IO (3)      | Identity and entropy are **data the composition           |\n   272\t|                                  | streams, linker, REPL secrets, custody, lease, await,     |             | supplies**; the driver deposits entropy on a stream       |\n   273\t|                                  | RPC; `rand`, `rand-int`; `SecureRandom` and twins.        |             | (§4.4). No callable generator in portable code (A2).      |\n   274\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   275\t| Clock                            | Driver only (`yin.repl.main`); `now` passed as data in    | IO (1,3)    | Unchanged; the contract names the driver's duty (§4.4).   |\n   276\t|                                  | `ws`.                                                     |             |                                                           |\n   277\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   278\t| Scheduling, wake-up, promises    | `dao.jing.content.async/default-schedule` and its self-   | IO (4)      | The async facade becomes a stepped state the driver       |\n   279\t|                                  | rescheduling pump (`:47-58, :100-149`); `btree.storage`   |             | pumps; the promise facade is driver-side composition code |\n   280\t|                                  | promise facade (`:218-227`); `waitset.driver` per host.   |             | (§4.4, H5). No thunk handed to a host timer from portable |\n   281\t|                                  |                                                           |             | code.                                                     |\n   282\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   283\t| Ambient properties               | `os.name`/`platform` in `store/fs.cljc:271-273`           | IO (1)      | A seam capability (`:directory-sync?`) and a driver fact  |\n   284\t|                                  | (directory-sync capability); `java.version`/Node version  |             | (`:host-banner`) supplied as data (H5).                   |\n   285\t|                                  | in `repl.cljc:275-277` (banner); `user.home` in           |             |                                                           |\n   286\t|                                  | `main.cljc:348`.                                          |             |                                                           |\n   287\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   288\t| Printing                         | `yin.repl.main` (driver); one `println` in                | IO (2)      | The one core site becomes an emitted value (H5).          |\n   289\t|                                  | `yang.python.antlr.repl:71` (V).                          |             |                                                           |\n   290\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   291\t| Threads, atomics, locks          | Driver and seams; `AtomicBoolean` (btree transients),     | Runtime     | Documented prerequisite (table C). Not a boundary.        |\n   292\t|                                  | `locking` on the JVM in five namespaces.                  | prereq.     |                                                           |\n   293\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   294\t| Exact integers, floats, bytes,   | §1 rows; two integer shims.                               | Pure        | Primitive profile, exact manifest §4.3 table A.           |\n   295\t| text, arrays                     |                                                           |             |                                                           |\n   296\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   297\t| Hashing, signing                 | `dao.jing:59-135`; `sign.cljc`.                           | Pure, in-   | Profile table A; `verify`/`sign` pure given the seed;     |\n   298\t|                                  |                                                           | instance    | seed from entropy data (§4.4).                            |\n   299\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   300\t| Canonical content codec (Jing    | Decode portable (`cbor.cljc:29-35`); writer via Boring or | Pure        | Portable writer over the profile (H4, OQ4 adopted).       |\n   301\t| CBOR writer)                     | the Dart `cbor` package.                                  |             |                                                           |\n   302\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   303\t| Carrier types with host equality | `yin.vm.values` `Closure`/`Continuation`; `dao.jing.cbor` | Runtime     | Table C; one documented per-host protocol block each,     |\n   304\t| hashing, printing                | `Float64`/`Rational`/`Decimal`.                           | prereq.     | with the equality and hash laws named (A4).               |\n   305\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   306\t| Transport codecs                 | Codec track; C0, C1 landed (V `git log` `8351e639`,       | --          | Owned there; untouched here.                              |\n   307\t|                                  | `eacaed90`).                                              |             |                                                           |\n   308\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   309\t| Python parser                    | Stage between streams; host walk per host.                | Either      | Stage's host adapter is a seam value; remote-stage test   |\n   310\t|                                  |                                                           | (§2.3)      | (H7).                                                     |\n   311\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   312\t| Dialect syntax                   | `catch` arms, hints, protocol names, `exists?` in ~40     | Not IO      | Exempt from the gate by documented pattern (§3.3).        |\n   313\t|                                  | files.                                                    |             |                                                           |\n   314\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   315\t| GUI, graphics, demos             | `dao.gui.*`, `dao.postgraphics.*`, `datomworld.demo.*`.   | --          | Out of the adopted scope (OQ1).                           |\n   316\t+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n   317\t\n   318\t### 3.2 Census of effect sources by resolved call, over the `yin.repl` closure (V)\n   319\t\n   320\tScope: `src/cljc` minus `dao/gui`, `dao/postgraphics`, `datomworld`, `world`\n   321\t(the adopted closure, OQ1). Method: `rg` for the call forms named in each\n   322\trow, 2026-10-20; every hit opened. This replaces r1's reader-conditional\n   323\tcensus as the enumeration the H0 gate is built from.\n   324\t\n   325\t+---+--------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------+\n   326\t| # | Source                         | Sites (file:line)                                                                                                | Slice |\n   327\t+===+================================+==================================================================================================================+=======+\n   328\t| 1 | `random-uuid` (identities,     | `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:27,185`; `memory_log.cljc:73`; `ws.cljc:122`; `remote.cljc:1249`;                    | H5    |\n   329\t|   | request prefixes, secrets,     | `remote_pair.cljc:180`; `remote_route.cljc:173`; `journal.cljc:296`; `dao/jing/content/step.cljc:132`;            |       |\n   330\t|   | temp names)                    | `dao/lease.cljc:594`; `dao/await.cljc:235,240`; `dao/space/store/fs.cljc:137,351`; `yin/vm/linker.cljc:1685`;      |       |\n   331\t|   |                                | `yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc:46`; `yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:1507`; `yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc:417,604,606`;   |       |\n   332\t|   |                                | `yin/vm/telemetry.cljc:112`; `yin/repl.cljc:667,668,733,918` (capability secret, secret source, macro token,       |       |\n   333\t|   |                                | shell token); `yin/repl/dht.cljc:117`. 24 sites.                                                                 |       |\n   334\t+---+--------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------+\n   335\t| 2 | `rand`, `rand-int`,            | `dao/stream/rpc.cljc:114-116` (request id); `dao/jing/dht.cljc:373` (query id); `dao/space/dht.cljc:142-151`      | H5    |\n   336\t|   | secure generators              | (node id, nonces); `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc:79,120` (seeds).                                                      |       |\n   337\t+---+--------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------+\n   338\t| 3 | `gensym` (process counter)     | `yang/clojure.cljc:349,359`; `yang/php.cljc:575`; `dao/space/transact.cljc:35`. (The VM's `:vm/gensym` is machine| H5    |\n   339\t|   |                                | state, `engine.cljc:2378`, deterministic: not a source.)                                                         |       |\n   340\t+---+--------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------+\n   341\t| 4 | Clock                          | `yin/repl/main.cljc:1242,1275,1408,1435,1542` (driver). None in the core.                                        | none  |\n   342\t+---+--------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------+\n   343\t| 5 | Ambient properties             | `dao/space/store/fs.cljc:92,136,271-273` (pid, kill-probe, os name); `yin/repl.cljc:275-277` (banner);           | H5,H6 |\n   344\t|   |                                | `yin/repl/main.cljc:348-349,880,959,1388,1459-1460,1483` (driver).                                               |       |\n   345\t+---+--------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------+\n   346\t| 6 | Printing, stdin                | `yin/repl/main.cljc` (19 sites, driver); `yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc:71` (core: one `println`).                 | H5    |\n   347\t+---+--------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------+\n   348\t| 7 | Timers, threads, promises      | `dao/jing/content/async.cljc:52-57`; `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc:224-227`; `yin/repl/main.cljc:1321,1343`         | H5    |\n   349\t|   |                                | (driver); `locking` in `jing/file.cljc:338`, `journal.cljc:86`, `transactor.cljc:113`, `schema.cljc:886`,         | (C)   |\n   350\t|   |                                | `ucf/authority.cljc:55` (JVM only; runtime prerequisite).                                                        |       |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
