ijn`\n   and `dao.jing.cbor`, this dimension defines no project-local Rational\n   carrier of its own to fill that gap, so Dart falls in with CLJS here.\"\n  #_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n  [v]\n  #?(:cljd false :cljs false :clj (ratio? v)))\n\n\n(defn- host-bigint?\n  \"Bigint is supported only where this repo already has a host-verified,\n   unambiguous predicate for it: `clojure.lang.BigInt` / `BigInteger` on\n   the JVM, distinct from `int?` (which is also true for both on the\n   JVM, so it cannot be used to tell them apart). `yin.vm.debruijn/\n   numeric-class` -- the existing repo pattern for cross-host numeric\n   classification -- does not attempt bigint detection on :cljd either\n   (its :cljd branch falls straight to double-class for anything\n   `int?` does not claim); this dimension matches that absence rather\n   than guess an unverified ClojureDart class name that could either\n   silently misclassify or fail to compile. A Dart or JS bigint value is\n   refused with :unsupported-value rather than encoded.\"\n  #_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n  [v]\n  #?(:cljd false\n     :cljs false\n     :clj (or (instance? clojure.lang.BigInt v) (instance? java.math.BigInteger v))))\n\n\n(defn- host-long?\n  \"A JVM boxed integral type; a CLJS safe integer (S2 item 4's own\n   wording); a Dart native int (`int?`), the same test `yin.vm.debruijn/\n   numeric-class` already uses for this host.\"\n  [v]\n  #?(:cljd (int? v)\n     :clj (or (instance? Long v) (instance? Integer v) (instance? Short v)\n              (instance? Byte v))\n     :cljs (and (number? v) (js/Number.isSafeInteger v))))\n\n\n(defn- host-double?\n  \"On the JVM, exactly `java.lang.Double` -- not 'every remaining number':\n   a JVM BigDecimal or Float is a distinct type this dimension's 14-class\n   domain does not declare, and folding either into :double would hash\n   its value at whatever precision `(double v)` happens to produce\n   instead of refusing it, exactly the silent canonicalization S2\n   forbids. On CLJS and CLJD, every remaining number: not a ratio, not a\n   bigint, not a long by this host's own rule -- CLJS has no BigDecimal/\n   Float distinction from a plain number to lose, so the complement rule\n   stays correct there. Jing's float64 carrier, how JS keeps an integral\n   float's kind, is :double too.\"\n  [v]\n  #?(:cljd (and (number? v) (not (host-long? v)))\n     :clj (instance? Double v)\n     :cljs (or (and (cbor/float64? v) (not (number? v)))\n               (and (number? v) (not (host-long? v)) (not (host-ratio? v))\n                    (not (host-bigint? v))))))\n\n\n                    (range (inc (min b t)) (max b t)))))\n        (keep (fn [pc]\n                (let [t (nth v pc)]\n                  (when (and (vector? t)\n                             (contains? #{:jump :branch-false}\n                                        (nth t 0)))\n                    [pc (nth t 1)])))\n              (range (count v)))))\n\n\n(defn- degraded-occurrences\n  \"The conservative degradation's own occurrence records (section 4.1):\n   every name retained at no position, inside a body -- a scanner that\n   cannot read positions retains every occurrence and discharges\n   nothing.\"\n  [names]\n  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :in-body? true}) names))))\n\n\n(defn- degraded-definitions\n  \"The conservative degradation's own definition records (section 4.1):\n   every key retained at no position, conditional -- a definition whose\n   position is unknown discharges nothing.\"\n  [names]\n  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :conditional? true})\n                     names))))\n\n\n(defn semantic-free-occurrences\n  \"Every free `:var` occurrence of canonical vector `v` as a section 4.1\n   record `{:name sym :at pc :in-body? b}`, in pc order (UCF section\n   7.3.2): a `:var` at pc `p` is bound iff `p` lies in the body of a\n                              (.closeSync ^js fs fd))))\n                     (when before-rename (before-rename temp))\n                     (.renameSync ^js fs temp target)\n                     (sync-directory! fs dir)\n                     (catch :default e\n                       (throw (ex-info (str \"cannot replace \" target \": \" e)\n                                       {:dir dir :target target}\n                                       e)))))))))\n\n\n(defn read-file-text\n(defn normalize-nfc\n  \"The one NFC seam of the projection (§5): every string entering\n   canonical encoding passes through here. :clj delegates to\n   java.text.Normalizer, :cljs to String.prototype.normalize, and :cljd\n   to the unorm_dart package (Unicode 16.0, owner-settled 2026-09-21) so\n   every ClojureDart target normalizes identically. NFC normalisation\n   collisions — distinct inputs with one composed form — are an\n   inherited limit of the repository encoding.\"\n  [^String s]\n  #?(:clj (java.text.Normalizer/normalize s java.text.Normalizer$Form/NFC)\n     :cljs (.normalize s \"NFC\")\n     :cljd (unorm/nfc s)))\n\n# yin.repl on jolt: implementation plan for the jolt host lane\n\nThis plan adds jolt (Clojure on Chez Scheme) as a fourth shared-source host lane\nfor yin.vm and yin.repl, next to the JVM, Node and Dart lanes. It is not another\nVM, not a source-to-jolt compiler and not a new dao.stream contract. The\nexisting semantic, register and stack machinery, frontend lowering, stream\ncontracts and conformance oracle stay shared. jolt branches are added only where\nthe host differs: exact integers, hashing, CBOR host values, files, signing,\nsockets, UDP and WebSocket. The standard frontend catalog is served by an\nin-process ANTLR4 C++ parser over FFI, with no fallback. The first milestone is\na local REPL (through J5). Host-lane parity, with native WebSocket and UDP/DHT,\nfollows at J8.\n\nStatus: design only; not implemented; nothing commissioned. This document\nconsolidates the architect plan r7\n(`collab/1792427226000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r7.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`),\nits independent review\n(`collab/1792427469000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r7.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md`,\nfindings W1-W9) and the owner decisions of 2026-10-19. The four design points\nthe review left open are ruled on in §13.4 (Architect, 2026-10-20; the owner\nmay overrule). Owner decisions remain the owner's; §13.3 is empty. The codec\ntrack ([dao.stream.codec.md](./dao.stream.codec.md)) is independent of this\ndocument and keeps its own owner questions; this document states only J6's\ndependency on it (§9.4).\n\nChange note 2026-10-20 (Architect: claude-fable-5-1,\n`collab/1792454059000-architect-jolt-design-points.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md`):\n§13.4 becomes \"Architect rulings (owner may overrule)\" and rules on the\nTransit require, the WebSocket substrate, the 1009/1006 expectation and the\ninitial pin; §4.2, §4.4, §5, §6.4, §9.2-§9.4, §9.6, §10.1, §12, Appendix A and\nAppendix B are updated to match. Licensing (\"local builds only for now; revisit\nbefore any distribution\") and wss:// (\"out; ws:// only\") are recorded as\nowner-settled in §13.1 and removed from §13.3. Nothing else changed; nothing\nwas commissioned.\n\nChange note 2026-10-20, later (Architect: claude-fable-5-1,\n`collab/1792454808000-architect-transit-decoupling.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md`):\nthe owner redirected ruling 1 with \"we should rethink dependency on transit\nnamespace. it should not require transit\". Ruling 1 is replaced: no shared\nnamespace requires `dao.stream.transit`; the portable domain moves to a\n39:(def ^:private default-ref-type\n40:  ;; §5.3: :soft on the JVM (memory-pressure-aware), :strong on cljs/cljd\n42:  #?(:cljd :strong\n44:     :cljs :strong))\n49:   ref-type         ; :strong | :soft | :weak | :test;\n64:             (or (:ref-type opts) default-ref-type)\n100:(defn- new-lease\n124:  \"A fresh Settings sharing bf/ref-type/storage with sett, carrying a live\n128:             (.-ref-type sett)\n129:             (new-lease)\n181:;; :test ref-type is the deterministic-eviction seam — clearable on demand,\n205:  \"Wrap a freshly faulted (or newly stored) node per the settings ref-type.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
